A||||7||Fiero_24||Fiero with 0 oil pressure||||9||
Z||000000||Fiero_24||08-17-2001||10:25 PM||||I posted earlier, but the subject was a little vauge.  My Fiero (87 GT) today dropped to 0 oil pressure.  I have barely 35 while giving the car gas.  I am assuming the oil pump went out, but have no idea yet.  I just replaced the oil pressure sending unit the day before, and the oil was changed 1000 miles ago.  Has anyone had this problem?  The Fiero is being towed home right now since you can hear the valves ticking from lack of oil.  I do have full oil in the car.  I also saw a little smoke coming out of the dipstick hole, and the oil fill hole.    <P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||9
Z||000001||maryjane||08-18-2001||12:00 AM||||I replied on this earlier, but will again to keep it bumped up. Maybe someone else can jump in & help. Have you recently changed over to synthetic oil? It carries dirt a lot better., maybe clogged the screen or filter if you did. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_24||08-18-2001||12:56 AM||||Thanks maryjane.  I did read the reply, but I want people to reply to this one so that people can find this topic easier than the other one.  Has anyone ever taken an oil pan out of a V6?  <P>Craig<BR><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||08-18-2001||12:32 PM||||Well, I always say "start with the basics."  Start by changing the oil filter.  You never know, suppose it's possible the filter's clogged and the bypass ain't working.  Not likely, but an oil filter doesn't cost much.  And then there's this fascinating tale....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>One evening in my 1987 Cavalier Z24 3.1 V6 (a direct descendant of the Fiero's 2.8), took a hard left turn and lost all oil pressure!  Stopped.  Checked oil level; it was fine.  Restarted car. <B>Loud</B> clicking from lifters.  Wonderful  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>Was on a side street now, so <B>nursed</B> it (i.e. - drove s-l-o-w-l-y) towards the restaurant I was going to anyway.  Clicking the whole time.  As I gently turned into the parking lot, the oil pressure unexpectedly returned.  A welcome surprise  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Ate, drank, made merry, had a good time.  No sense worrying about damage already done.<P>Thought about asking for a ride home, but took my car home anyway.  Checked oil level -it was quite low.  Changed oil filter and topped off oil.  Still stumped as to what the problem had been.<P>I suddenly remembered that earlier that day, I was forced into running over a beer bottle (no room to change lanes - oh, well) that was standing upright in the street.  The oil filter in the Cav is right in front, and located just about where the beer bottle impacted.  Examined the old oil filter - it was dented ever so slightly, and had two very tiny holes in it!  Haven't had oil pressure problems in that car since  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sorry about the long story, but your situation reminded me of my trouble - hope it turns out to be something simple  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero_24||08-18-2001||03:39 PM||||Thanks for the info.  I am having my mechanic friend (he works for volvo) over to check it out.  We are going to take the oil filter off and take a good look, and what ever else to find the problem.<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||14
Z||000005||Fiero_24||08-18-2001||07:32 PM||||UPDATE!!!!!!!!!!<P>Tried changing the oil and filter.  I added 20w 50 since it only has to last me 1-2 months until the new motor is in.  I started it up and it was smooth, no knocks.  I drove it and it was fine.  I parked it and let it idle while I cleaned up.  The pressure was at 40 at idle, then the gauge started flickering after 20 minutes of running.  It now drops right above the red, but not in the red.  The oil pump is working.  I tested it by taking the oil filter off and disconnecting the ignition coil.  I then rotated the engine, and it spits oil.  It is quiet now.  You cannot hear the liters ticking any more.  Any other suggestions?<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||8
Z||000006||maryjane||08-18-2001||07:59 PM||||Just curious, whats the coolant temp when the oil press starts dropping? And if it keeps giving you trouble, try flushing out the oil pan. If prev owners didn't take care of it, sludge can build up and it starts getting sucked up onto strainer after it runs awhile. I've seen a lot of old gasket mtl and bits of silicone in pans when I've dropped them. Baby that sucker till you get the eng swap done. good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fiero_24||08-18-2001||08:22 PM||||It is running around 200 on the temp gauge after 20 minutes of running.  I am not planning on driving it until the new motor comes.  Just have to find different ways to get around until then.  The oil is pretty clean though, no shavings after straining the oil.  Even the top of the valves under the oil fill cap look clean.  I may even be a bad ring on a piston and after it warms up it produces blow by, but I am not sure on that.<BR>  <BR>Craig<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
